NEW MECHANISM GATE. Which extent `for_row_pairs` reserves is invisible in the
decoded pixels, so it gets its own coverage in `row_guard_policy_tests`, both
branches, plus a liveness test that it really yields both rows of every pair in
the right order (without which the extent assertions would pass for a helper
that silently yielded `None` and touched half the rows).

TEETH BY MUTATION. Each planted, confirmed failing, restored from a sha256
snapshot, re-verified green:

  pad fill `last` -> `0`                     cfl_ac parity FAILS 3/3 depths
  hull branch pairs row r with itself        cfl_ac parity FAILS 3/3 depths
  for_row_pairs `tile_threading_active()`
    -> `false` (hull always)                 threading-ON gate FAILS
    -> `true`  (per-row always)              threading-OFF child gate FAILS

PRE-EXISTING GATES re-proved to still have teeth on THIS tree, under
`--features __probe_wide` (a gate this change made unreachable would be a
regression even with everything green):

  (a) the 4af62ae lock-ordering TOCTOU — `add`'s IN-LOCK `state` re-read deleted
      -> `wide_exclusion` FAILS ("a narrow mutable borrow was granted inside a
      wide mutable borrow that was provably still held").
  (b) `active()` cut TO ONE shard -> `wide_exclusion` FAILS, same assertion.
  Restored both by sha256 -c AND `git diff --exit-code`; green after.

`#![forbid(unsafe_code)]` proved ACTIVELY, not by reading the attribute: a
planted `unsafe { core::ptr::null::<u8>().read() }` in src/decode.rs fails the
default build with "usage of an `unsafe` block"; restored, rebuild green.


6. NOT MEASURED / STILL OPEN
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6a. DESIGN B WAS NOT BUILT and is not recommended by this round's data either.
    Its ceiling (the whole tracker at t=1: 51.2 ms at 8bpc, 58.8 at 10bpc) is
    still only a ceiling; its own share was never measured, by anyone.
6b. THE t>1 COMPACT COPY IS STILL THERE and is still unmeasured. Above one
    thread `block_mut` takes the Compact path: `compact_read_per_row` (h
    registrations + a memcpy in) and `BlockMut::drop` ->
    `compact_write_back_per_row` (h more + a memcpy out) — 2,662,876 +
    1,864,816 registrations/frame at t=8 plus two memcpys per block, existing
    ONLY because per-row guards are needed. A real static split would delete
    the copy too. Nobody has priced the copy.
6c. THE LARGEST REMAINING LEVERS, from this round's fresh census of ee07b00:
      t=1 (7,363,488 total): ctx.rs:99 CaseSetter::set_disjoint 2,534,988 (34%)
          — #467 §5b, sub-64-KiB BlockContext instances, needs a concurrency
          argument about `f.a[t.a]` that nobody has established.
      t=8 (22,700,725): loopfilter.rs:566 3,835,042 (17%);
          picture.rs:1997 BlockMut write-back 2,662,876 (12%);
          ctx.rs:99 2,534,988 (11%);
          picture.rs:168 `with_pixel_guard_immut` per-row 2,336,708 (10%) —
          that one is `ipred_prepare`'s LEFT-COLUMN read at w=1, i.e. 2.3 M
          single-BYTE registrations. A column is not an interval, so no hull
          can cover it; it would need a strided registration primitive in the
          tracker itself.
6d. NEITHER DESIGN CLEARS t=8 AND NEITHER CAN. The untracked ceiling is 1.339
    (8bpc) / 1.390 (10bpc). Whatever closes t=8 is not tracker work. This round
    changes nothing about that.
6e. ONLY `v4k_8tile` / `v4k_8tile_10b`, only t=1/2/4/8, only aarch64. No
    x86_64 build or run. Both 4K vectors are intra-only with loop restoration
    OFF, so `mc_arm.rs` and `looprestoration*.rs` register ZERO borrows in this
    grid while LR is active in 696 of 768 corpus vectors — the same structural
    blindness AGENT_BRIEF §2 warns about, inherited unchanged.
6f. `cfl_ac`'s scalar counterpart (`src/ipred.rs::cfl_ac_rust`) is NOT
    converted; only the NEON dispatch path is. The scalar path runs when the
    Arm64 token is absent or `Family::IntraPred` is ablated.
